\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Toy endosymbiosis model, rendered with pyCOT's native reaction-network visualizer (bipartite species/reaction graph via \texttt  {rn\_visualize.py}). \textbf  {(a)} Host alone (glycolysis + fermentation). \textbf  {(b)} Symbiont alone (glycolysis + oxidative phosphorylation + Fe--S cluster biogenesis). \textbf  {(c)} Merged network; the three curated interface reactions (\texttt  {XPORT\_PYR}, \texttt  {XPORT\_ATP}, \texttt  {XPORT\_FES}) connect the two halves, and the two species reachable only once merged (orange) are exactly the ones the toy model was designed around.}}{3}{figure.caption.1}\protected@file@percent }
